        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 12 Word Processing and More with LibreOffice\nP\u00e1ginas: 235-268\n\u2022 Installing the LibreOffice Suite  (236)\n\u2022 Word Processing with LibreOffice Writer  (237)\n  \u2022 Taking a tour of LibreOffice Writer  (237)\n  \u2022 Working with Writer files  (241)\n\u2022 Spreadsheets with LibreOffice Calc  (242)\n  \u2022 Taking a tour of LibreOffice Calc  (242)\n  \u2022 Working with Calc files  (246)\n\u2022 Presentations with LibreOffice Impress  (246)\n  \u2022 Creating a new presentation  (247)\n  \u2022 Taking a tour of LibreOffice Impress  (247)\n  \u2022 Working with Impress files  (251)\n\u2022 Fine Art with LibreOffice Draw  (252)\n  \u2022 Taking a tour of LibreOffice Draw  (252)\n  \u2022 Working with Draw files  (255)\n\u2022 Managing Data with LibreOffice Base  (256)\n  \u2022 Getting help from the wizard  (256)\n  \u2022 Taking a tour of LibreOffice Base  (259)\n  \u2022 Sitting down at the table  (261)\n\u2022 Layout with LibreOffice Math  (262)\n  \u2022 Menu bar  (263)\n  \u2022 Standard toolbar  (264)\n  \u2022 Document section  (265)\nChapter 12\nWord Processing and\nMore with LibreOffice\nT\nhese days, just about everyone who has a computer has at least one office\nsuite at their fingertips. If they\u2019re Microsoft Windows users, this suite is\nprobably Microsoft Office, although it may be another worthy contender,\nsuch as Corel WordPerfect Office, or if your PC is connected to the Internet, the\nGoogle suite of programs. In Linux, typically the suite is LibreOffice, which has\nseparate programs for word processing, spreadsheets, presentations, and even\nworking with databases.\nAfter you figure out how to use one of the programs in this suite, you may be\nhappy to find that the others are designed to look and work in very similar ways.\nYou can even open and save files in Microsoft Office format, if you need to share\nthem with people who are using it \u2014 and you can edit the Office files people send\nyou, too.",
